{"step": 128, "tokens": 2096128, "dev_nll": 2.713191887844517, "arc": 17, "arc_preds": "DBABDAAAACADBCCBCCBB", "eval_s": 40.111462354660034, "generations": ["1. Assign specific cleaning tasks to each household member based on their schedule and preferences.\n2. Establish a daily routine where everyone washes their dishes immediately after use to prevent buildup.\n3. Keep a well-stocked supply of cleaning supplies and sponges in a central, easily accessible location.<|im_end|>", "To solve this problem, we can use a system of linear equations based on the number of heads and legs.\n\n**1. Define the variables:**\n*   Let $c$ be the number of chickens.\n*   Let $r$ be the number of rabbits.\n\n**2. Set up the equations:**\n*   **Heads:** Each animal has 1 head.\n    $$c + r = 10$$\n*   **Legs:** Chickens have 2 legs, and rabbits have 4 legs.\n    $$2c + 4r = 28$$\n\n**3", "```python\ndef is_balanced(text):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks whether parentheses are balanced in the given text,\n    ignoring all other characters.\n    \n    Args:\n        text (str): The input string to check.\n        \n    Returns:\n        bool: True if parentheses are balanced, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    stack = []\n    \n    for char in text:\n        if char == '(':\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char == ')':\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n            stack.pop()\n    \n    return len(stack) == 0\n", "\u0130\u015fte c\u00fcmlenizin daha resmi ve profesyonel bir T\u00fcrk\u00e7e kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131:\n\n\"Yar\u0131n kat\u0131lamayaca\u011f\u0131m; toplant\u0131y\u0131 erteleme imkan\u0131 var m\u0131?\"\n\nAlternatif olarak, e-posta veya daha kurumsal bir yaz\u0131\u015fmada \u015fu \u015fekilde de ifade edilebilir:\n\n\"Yar\u0131n kat\u0131l\u0131m\u0131m m\u00fcmk\u00fcn olmamaktad\u0131r; toplant\u0131y\u0131 erteleme talebinizle ilgili g\u00f6r\u00fc\u015fme yapabilir miyiz?\"<|im_end|>"]}
